1
00:00:00,733 --> 00:00:02,167
This is Kobayakawa Sota.

2
00:00:02,267 --> 00:00:02,867
My boyfriend.

3
00:00:02,967 --> 00:00:03,733
A tutor?

4
00:00:03,833 --> 00:00:04,833
Sick 'em, Rock.

5
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,476
Let's compromise. How about "Na-chan"?

6
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:08,500
Na...

7
00:00:08,567 --> 00:00:09,933
Whatever, call me what you want.

8
00:00:10,033 --> 00:00:11,667
You really like clouds, don't you?

9
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:14,467
My heart isn't racing.

10
00:00:14,667 --> 00:00:16,667
No, absolutely not.

11
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:27,033
"Your Summer, My Storm"
(Episode 3)

12
00:00:36,233 --> 00:00:37,400
Ever since I was little,

13
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,500
I've had a tendency to like
whatever my sister likes.

14
00:00:46,333 --> 00:00:48,067
If she danced...

15
00:00:48,493 --> 00:00:50,026
I wanted to dance too.

16
00:00:50,632 --> 00:00:53,232
- Huh, you too?
- We even liked the same anime characters.

17
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:53,633
So cool.

18
00:00:53,733 --> 00:00:55,433
- Stop copying me.
- Who's copying you?

19
00:00:55,533 --> 00:00:56,700
I just like it.

20
00:00:58,333 --> 00:00:59,000
But,

21
00:00:59,233 --> 00:01:02,100
I've never liked any of the guys
she's dated.

22
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:06,209
There was the guy with the killer glare who
looked ready to throw a punch at any second.

23
00:01:06,233 --> 00:01:09,133
The foreigner who couldn't
speak a word of Japanese.

24
00:01:09,233 --> 00:01:12,200
And the unsmiling, totally
unapproachable upperclassman.

25
00:01:12,433 --> 00:01:13,500
So this time, at first,

26
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:17,067
- Rio, over here.
- I thought he was just an annoying show-off.

27
00:01:17,833 --> 00:01:18,833
But now...

28
00:01:20,467 --> 00:01:22,633
If you calculate it like this,

29
00:01:22,733 --> 00:01:25,813
- you'll get the right answer.
- I'm starting to think he might be a good guy.

30
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:26,633
Are you listening?

31
00:01:26,733 --> 00:01:28,500
- Wow.
- We're slowly getting closer.

32
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:30,500
Can I tell you my story?

33
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Slowly.

34
00:01:32,333 --> 00:01:34,733
Na-chan.

35
00:01:35,167 --> 00:01:36,367
Slowly...

36
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:38,500
Huh?

37
00:01:39,367 --> 00:01:40,367
Slowly...

38
00:01:41,567 --> 00:01:42,267
What?

39
00:01:42,367 --> 00:01:43,400
Natsuki.

40
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:45,000
Do you want more watermelon?

41
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:46,200
What is this feeling...

42
00:01:47,333 --> 00:01:48,367
What's going on?

43
00:01:49,367 --> 00:01:50,367
Natsuki?

44
00:01:54,267 --> 00:01:55,267
Huh?

45
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:01,700
(Things look sparkly)

46
00:02:03,433 --> 00:02:04,433
What?

47
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:08,433
It could be a migraine
aura or an eye problem.

48
00:02:10,667 --> 00:02:12,100
Hey.

49
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:19,000
(Other possible causes)

50
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:20,100
(Love)

51
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:21,133
Lo...

52
00:02:21,467 --> 00:02:22,467
Love?

53
00:02:25,167 --> 00:02:27,667
No way...

54
00:02:28,267 --> 00:02:30,000
That guy is my sister's boyfriend.

55
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:30,967
Hello.

56
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:32,100
Whoa!

57
00:02:32,433 --> 00:02:33,167
You scared me to death.

58
00:02:33,267 --> 00:02:35,200
That's my line.

59
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:36,500
What's wrong with you?

60
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:37,633
Are you feeling sick?

61
00:02:38,433 --> 00:02:39,967
No, not at all.

62
00:02:40,333 --> 00:02:42,533
But you've been acting
weird for a while now.

63
00:02:43,033 --> 00:02:44,367
Have I?

64
00:02:44,467 --> 00:02:46,300
Muttering to yourself over here.

65
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:49,176
I thought you were going to eat the watermelon,
but you just picked it up and put it down.

66
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:51,240
And your facial expressions
are all over the place.

67
00:02:51,433 --> 00:02:53,333
Was I doing that?

68
00:02:53,433 --> 00:02:55,433
Don't tell me you studied
so hard you got a fever?

69
00:02:55,567 --> 00:02:56,033
What?

70
00:02:56,133 --> 00:02:59,133
You suddenly started studying so hard
that your body couldn't keep up.

71
00:02:59,233 --> 00:03:00,567
Is that why you have a fever?

72
00:03:01,267 --> 00:03:02,267
I'm not a kid.

73
00:03:02,333 --> 00:03:03,333
Oh, watermelon.

74
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:04,633
Thanks for the food.

75
00:03:04,733 --> 00:03:06,000
Hey, what are you doing?

76
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:10,233
So good.

77
00:03:10,333 --> 00:03:11,900
I was just about to eat that.

78
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,433
There's plenty more.

79
00:03:14,267 --> 00:03:15,567
Rio, are you heading out?

80
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,233
Yeah, on a date.

81
00:03:17,333 --> 00:03:18,200
With Sota-san?

82
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:19,300
Yep.

83
00:03:19,859 --> 00:03:20,859
Natsuki.

84
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:22,967
I heard you still can't call him "So-chan"?

85
00:03:23,067 --> 00:03:23,467
Huh?

86
00:03:23,567 --> 00:03:26,233
Sota said he can already call you Na-chan.

87
00:03:26,846 --> 00:03:29,252
Na-chan.

88
00:03:30,533 --> 00:03:33,600
It's just a name.
Why are you so shy about it?

89
00:03:34,167 --> 00:03:35,700
I... I'm not shy.

90
00:03:36,433 --> 00:03:37,667
Here, enjoy.

91
00:03:38,567 --> 00:03:39,567
Thanks.

92
00:03:41,367 --> 00:03:42,367
Coming.

93
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:52,300
Today,

94
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:54,760
Sota and I are going to the
National Museum of Western Art.

95
00:03:55,067 --> 00:03:56,067
Oh, really?

96
00:03:57,067 --> 00:03:58,133
You know, Sota

97
00:03:58,667 --> 00:04:01,400
didn't even know it's
actually a World Heritage Site.

98
00:04:02,967 --> 00:04:04,700
He looks like he knows everything,

99
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:07,300
but he's surprisingly clueless sometimes.

100
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:11,567
Does he only know a lot
about the things he likes?

101
00:04:12,033 --> 00:04:13,033
Yeah.

102
00:04:13,367 --> 00:04:15,533
Like when he talks
about his favorite bridges,

103
00:04:15,967 --> 00:04:18,100
he's like a walking encyclopedia.

104
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:20,433
And he talks faster and
faster once he gets going.

105
00:04:20,633 --> 00:04:23,900
Bridges can cross rivers, oceans,
valleys, and roads,

106
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,333
connecting two places that
were originally separated.

107
00:04:28,067 --> 00:04:29,967
But that part of him is really cute.

108
00:04:31,746 --> 00:04:32,746
Cute, huh...

109
00:04:33,633 --> 00:04:35,167
Sota is cute, isn't he?

110
00:04:38,053 --> 00:04:41,453
Kaoru-san brought some
bread from her bakery.

111
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:43,420
Rio, do you want to take some on your date?

112
00:04:43,567 --> 00:04:44,633
Sure, why not?

113
00:04:44,733 --> 00:04:46,200
Pick whatever you like.

114
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:47,533
Awesome.

115
00:04:49,367 --> 00:04:50,433
Oh, melon bread.

116
00:04:50,533 --> 00:04:51,867
- Wow, there's a lot.
- Yeah.

117
00:04:51,967 --> 00:04:53,167
They all look so good.

118
00:04:53,267 --> 00:04:54,733
Where should we eat them?

119
00:04:55,233 --> 00:04:58,000
After the museum, we're
going to look at bridges.

120
00:04:58,200 --> 00:04:59,333
- Bridges?
- Yeah.

121
00:04:59,433 --> 00:05:01,567
I was just telling Natsuki about it.

122
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:04,933
Sota loves bridges and
knows so much about them.

123
00:05:05,033 --> 00:05:06,033
That's pretty rare.

124
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:06,633
Right?

125
00:05:06,733 --> 00:05:11,133
It feels like you're getting to know each other through
the history and romance of World Heritage Sites.

126
00:05:11,367 --> 00:05:13,100
Exactly.

127
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:14,333
Oh, and then,

128
00:05:14,567 --> 00:05:17,533
Sota said he wants to be a
bridge builder in the future.

129
00:05:17,633 --> 00:05:20,233
Oh my, how cool.

130
00:05:20,333 --> 00:05:22,100
The reason he came to our university

131
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:25,276
is apparently because there's a professor who's
quite famous in the field of architecture.

132
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:26,467
I see.

133
00:05:26,567 --> 00:05:28,300
That makes him sound even cooler.

134
00:05:29,167 --> 00:05:31,033
Oh right, the pot.

135
00:05:34,773 --> 00:05:35,773
Um,

136
00:05:38,567 --> 00:05:43,200
isn't it better not to talk about someone's
dreams or private matters when they aren't around?

137
00:05:43,667 --> 00:05:44,667
Really?

138
00:05:45,667 --> 00:05:49,433
Maybe those are things
he only wanted you to know.

139
00:05:52,846 --> 00:05:53,846
I see.

140
00:05:57,100 --> 00:05:59,367
I'm the type to just blurt everything out,

141
00:06:00,067 --> 00:06:01,733
so sometimes I really don't notice.

142
00:06:03,633 --> 00:06:05,000
Thanks for telling me.

143
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:09,467
Thanks a bunch.

144
00:06:09,567 --> 00:06:10,567
Hey, stop that.

145
00:06:10,667 --> 00:06:11,533
- Take this.
- No.

146
00:06:11,633 --> 00:06:12,933
- Don't be shy.
- Stop it.

147
00:06:13,033 --> 00:06:14,067
Get away from me.

148
00:06:15,133 --> 00:06:16,433
By the way, that's my shirt.

149
00:06:16,967 --> 00:06:17,433
Looks good, right?

150
00:06:17,533 --> 00:06:18,633
Don't steal my clothes.

151
00:06:18,733 --> 00:06:20,367
But I really like it.

152
00:06:20,467 --> 00:06:21,300
That's mine.

153
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:22,400
(Open)

154
00:06:22,667 --> 00:06:24,867
(Closed)

155
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:25,967
- Go for it.
- Oh crap.

156
00:06:26,033 --> 00:06:27,500
Nice.

157
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:28,500
What the heck.

158
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:30,567
- Yeah, see that?
- Damn it.

159
00:06:30,667 --> 00:06:32,367
Hey, Natsuki, shouldn't you be studying?

160
00:06:32,467 --> 00:06:34,067
Look who's talking.

161
00:06:34,167 --> 00:06:35,000
Anyway, hurry up and help out.

162
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:36,543
I need to take a break sometimes, okay?

163
00:06:36,567 --> 00:06:38,076
Besides, my tutor isn't
coming until tonight.

164
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:39,100
Oh right, that tutor.

165
00:06:39,179 --> 00:06:40,746
He doesn't seem that annoying.

166
00:06:40,853 --> 00:06:41,286
Huh?

167
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:42,600
Did you meet him?

168
00:06:42,933 --> 00:06:44,966
We saw him last time.

169
00:06:45,967 --> 00:06:47,567
We saw you guys walking together.

170
00:06:47,787 --> 00:06:48,787
What?

171
00:06:50,433 --> 00:06:52,333
You looked really happy, Natsuki.

172
00:06:52,433 --> 00:06:53,433
Yeah.

173
00:06:53,567 --> 00:06:55,267
You guys looked like best buds.

174
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:57,233
What? N-No way.

175
00:06:58,033 --> 00:06:59,533
That's impossible.

176
00:07:02,813 --> 00:07:03,913
Sorry to keep you waiting.

177
00:07:05,567 --> 00:07:06,567
No worries.

178
00:07:07,033 --> 00:07:08,133
Let's go.

179
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,467
I'm so excited.

180
00:07:10,567 --> 00:07:12,000
Yeah.

181
00:07:13,167 --> 00:07:14,167
Okay.

182
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:16,700
Sota.

183
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:19,000
It's this way.

184
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:20,100
Huh?

185
00:07:21,746 --> 00:07:22,746
Ah.

186
00:07:23,892 --> 00:07:25,052
I was holding it upside down.

187
00:07:27,633 --> 00:07:29,967
You're not very good at reading maps, Sota.

188
00:07:30,067 --> 00:07:32,333
That's not true. I just misread it.

189
00:07:32,633 --> 00:07:33,643
You really are a bit clueless.

190
00:07:33,667 --> 00:07:35,167
No, I'm not.

191
00:07:35,633 --> 00:07:37,100
I'm saying you're cute.

192
00:07:37,886 --> 00:07:38,886
Cu...

193
00:07:39,233 --> 00:07:40,233
Cute?

194
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:47,200
Wh... What do you mean by cute?

195
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:48,033
Exactly what it sounds like.

196
00:07:48,133 --> 00:07:48,900
I'm home.

197
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,633
- Oh, Rock.
- Welcome back.

198
00:07:51,267 --> 00:07:53,200
How was the soba-making class?

199
00:07:54,267 --> 00:07:55,367
It was alright, I guess.

200
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:59,100
Could it become a retirement hobby?

201
00:07:59,367 --> 00:08:00,967
That remains to be seen.

202
00:08:01,067 --> 00:08:02,600
Huh, what about Fuku-chan?

203
00:08:02,700 --> 00:08:03,967
Did he manage to make any?

204
00:08:04,067 --> 00:08:07,100
The teacher practically
did everything for him.

205
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:10,733
Wow, he's pretty shrewd.

206
00:08:12,533 --> 00:08:13,600
Where are the kids?

207
00:08:14,433 --> 00:08:15,433
Did they go out?

208
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:16,500
Yeah.

209
00:08:16,567 --> 00:08:17,567
Natsuki too?

210
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,200
He needs some fresh air once in a while.

211
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:23,900
Can he really afford to be so laid-back?

212
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:29,067
But Sota-san said
Natsuki is working really hard.

213
00:08:29,091 --> 00:08:31,657
And he's a fast learner.

214
00:08:32,233 --> 00:08:33,400
Oh, really?

215
00:08:33,633 --> 00:08:38,033
Rio really found him a great tutor.

216
00:08:38,133 --> 00:08:39,213
They're about the same age.

217
00:08:39,567 --> 00:08:40,567
And they're both guys.

218
00:08:41,213 --> 00:08:42,322
They probably get along well.

219
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:43,533
Yeah.

220
00:08:47,633 --> 00:08:48,533
Delicious.

221
00:08:48,633 --> 00:08:52,367
Uncle, your ramen and
gyoza are the best in the world.

222
00:08:52,467 --> 00:08:53,367
No.

223
00:08:53,453 --> 00:08:54,595
The best in the world is the yurinchi.

224
00:08:54,633 --> 00:08:55,233
No way.

225
00:08:55,333 --> 00:08:57,500
You guys need to broaden your horizons.

226
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:00,133
Natsuki and Ryo really
appreciate my cooking.

227
00:09:00,233 --> 00:09:01,267
Yeah.

228
00:09:01,367 --> 00:09:02,533
Unlike my foolish son.

229
00:09:02,633 --> 00:09:04,200
What? Foolish son?

230
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:05,900
You should be more honest too.

231
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:06,567
Exactly.

232
00:09:06,667 --> 00:09:07,533
It's really good.

233
00:09:07,633 --> 00:09:09,009
It's so good, I want to eat it every day.

234
00:09:09,033 --> 00:09:10,733
- Yeah.
- You two are definitely siblings.

235
00:09:10,946 --> 00:09:12,980
Rio said the exact same thing last time.

236
00:09:13,073 --> 00:09:13,706
Huh?

237
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,600
Mmm, so delicious!

238
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:16,533
So good!

239
00:09:16,633 --> 00:09:17,967
I want to eat this every day.

240
00:09:18,167 --> 00:09:19,033
Yummy.

241
00:09:19,133 --> 00:09:21,000
And then she actually
came two days in a row.

242
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:22,576
And she brought a guy
with her on the second day.

243
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:23,867
Wait, really?

244
00:09:23,967 --> 00:09:24,567
Huh, is that so?

245
00:09:24,667 --> 00:09:26,467
I wasn't there, you were
the one who told me!

246
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:29,580
Did she come with her boyfriend?

247
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:33,267
I can't violate my customers' privacy.

248
00:09:33,467 --> 00:09:35,507
It's the professional code
of the service industry.

249
00:09:36,106 --> 00:09:36,607
Well said, Uncle.

250
00:09:36,632 --> 00:09:38,782
What are you talking
about? Just admit you forgot.

251
00:09:38,967 --> 00:09:41,100
Ah, could it be Natsuki's tutor?

252
00:09:42,033 --> 00:09:46,000
Was the guy with her
a smiling, cheerful monster?

253
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:47,500
Ah, exactly like that.

254
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,167
What do you mean by "cheerful monster"?

255
00:09:49,267 --> 00:09:51,233
Well said, Natsuki.

256
00:09:51,333 --> 00:09:52,000
What's so good about it?

257
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:53,643
- It's alright.
- Eat up, the best in the world.

258
00:09:53,667 --> 00:09:54,567
It's really delicious.

259
00:09:54,667 --> 00:09:57,600
I mean, was I just feeling disappointed?

260
00:09:57,700 --> 00:10:01,367
Thinking, "So my sister
and he went on a date here"?

261
00:10:03,126 --> 00:10:04,126
Why though?

262
00:10:13,833 --> 00:10:15,899
You really like clouds, don't you?

263
00:10:18,367 --> 00:10:20,367
Why am I remembering this?

264
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:23,467
Get out of my head!

265
00:10:23,733 --> 00:10:25,333
Na-chan.

266
00:10:26,633 --> 00:10:28,500
I told you to keep it down.

267
00:10:29,033 --> 00:10:30,200
Na-chan.

268
00:10:33,340 --> 00:10:34,340
Huh?

269
00:10:35,467 --> 00:10:36,467
Give me a sec.

270
00:10:37,733 --> 00:10:39,200
It's the real him.

271
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:45,700
Fancy running into you.

272
00:10:47,667 --> 00:10:49,467
Huh, where's my sister?

273
00:10:49,567 --> 00:10:50,733
She went to work.

274
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:52,433
I see.

275
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:55,033
How was the art museum?

276
00:10:55,273 --> 00:10:57,306
It was awesome.

277
00:10:57,633 --> 00:10:58,633
Let me tell you.

278
00:10:58,686 --> 00:11:00,819
There was a painting
called "Bridge in the Sky."

279
00:11:01,567 --> 00:11:04,533
The bridge was surrounded
by clouds under a fiery sunset.

280
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:06,933
Man.

281
00:11:07,033 --> 00:11:09,967
I really wish you
could've seen it, Na-chan.

282
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:11,700
Oh, really?

283
00:11:13,913 --> 00:11:14,913
Pop quiz.

284
00:11:15,267 --> 00:11:16,367
Huh, so sudden?

285
00:11:16,733 --> 00:11:19,467
Why do summer sunsets turn red?

286
00:11:20,167 --> 00:11:23,333
Because there's more water
vapor in the air during summer.

287
00:11:23,567 --> 00:11:24,600
Spot on.

288
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:26,533
You really know your weather.

289
00:11:26,633 --> 00:11:28,233
No, that's just basic knowledge.

290
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:29,600
Don't underestimate me.

291
00:11:30,567 --> 00:11:32,467
Na-chan, are you a punk?

292
00:11:32,567 --> 00:11:33,233
What?

293
00:11:33,333 --> 00:11:34,100
No way.

294
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:35,367
I'm not that cocky.

295
00:11:36,533 --> 00:11:39,333
What does "cocky" mean?

296
00:11:39,733 --> 00:11:40,733
Huh?

297
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,367
You don't know?

298
00:11:45,606 --> 00:11:46,639
I'm home.

299
00:11:46,926 --> 00:11:48,260
Pardon the intrusion.

300
00:11:48,433 --> 00:11:49,433
Huh?

301
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:51,400
Is Rock not here?

302
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:56,567
Natsuki.

303
00:11:56,667 --> 00:11:58,000
- Welcome back.
- I'm home.

304
00:11:58,100 --> 00:11:59,633
Welcome, Sota-san.

305
00:11:59,733 --> 00:12:01,200
Thanks for having me again today.

306
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:03,567
We're the ones who should be thanking you.

307
00:12:03,667 --> 00:12:05,000
Mom, where's Rock?

308
00:12:05,212 --> 00:12:06,413
Isn't he sleeping over there?

309
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:17,600
No, he's not.

310
00:12:18,067 --> 00:12:19,333
That can't be.

311
00:12:20,067 --> 00:12:22,133
Did Dad take him for a walk?

312
00:12:22,233 --> 00:12:25,600
Fuku-chan dragged your dad out for drinks.

313
00:12:29,753 --> 00:12:30,753
Rock!

314
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:34,233
Rock!

315
00:12:35,733 --> 00:12:36,467
Did you find him?

316
00:12:36,567 --> 00:12:37,367
No.

317
00:12:37,467 --> 00:12:38,576
- Huh?
- Can't find him anywhere.

318
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:39,600
What? No way.

319
00:12:39,667 --> 00:12:40,900
This is too weird.

320
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,267
Wait, how could this happen?

321
00:12:42,367 --> 00:12:45,133
Rock!

322
00:12:45,233 --> 00:12:46,667
Huh, how is this possible?

323
00:12:47,267 --> 00:12:48,067
Where did he go?

324
00:12:48,167 --> 00:12:49,167
Um.

325
00:12:49,191 --> 00:12:50,711
Let's calm down and retrace our steps.

326
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:53,000
Yeah, you're right.

327
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:56,167
Ma'am, have you been home this whole time?

328
00:12:57,033 --> 00:12:59,567
I went out for groceries and just got back.

329
00:12:59,667 --> 00:13:01,067
Did you see Rock when you got back?

330
00:13:01,133 --> 00:13:01,867
Was he here?

331
00:13:01,967 --> 00:13:02,967
No.

332
00:13:03,067 --> 00:13:04,300
I'm home.

333
00:13:04,324 --> 00:13:05,357
Rock?

334
00:13:06,167 --> 00:13:08,200
He didn't come to the door to greet me.

335
00:13:08,533 --> 00:13:12,533
But sometimes he just sleeps like a log
in the room, right?

336
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,033
So I figured I shouldn't bother him.

337
00:13:15,133 --> 00:13:17,233
And I didn't check if he was there.

338
00:13:17,667 --> 00:13:21,700
What about before that?
Was he here before you left?

339
00:13:22,233 --> 00:13:22,533
Yeah.

340
00:13:22,633 --> 00:13:23,400
I'm heading out.

341
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:25,700
He saw me off at the door.

342
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:28,500
Which means...

343
00:13:28,533 --> 00:13:32,267
He went missing while
you were out shopping.

344
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:34,700
Ah.

345
00:13:35,067 --> 00:13:36,633
- Huh?
- Did you remember something?

346
00:13:36,733 --> 00:13:37,733
The door lock.

347
00:13:38,333 --> 00:13:40,300
I thought I'd be right back.

348
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:42,533
So I left without locking the door.

349
00:13:42,633 --> 00:13:43,633
So that's why Rock...

350
00:13:43,733 --> 00:13:46,533
Wait, can Rock open doors by himself?

351
00:13:47,167 --> 00:13:48,267
No, he can't.

352
00:13:48,367 --> 00:13:51,100
Could someone have opened the door
and let Rock out?

353
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:54,233
Or did someone come in and take him?

354
00:13:54,333 --> 00:13:57,300
He shouldn't just go with a stranger.

355
00:13:57,733 --> 00:13:59,200
It's possible, though.

356
00:13:59,533 --> 00:14:00,676
Rock is really friendly, after all.

357
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:02,233
This is all my fault.

358
00:14:02,333 --> 00:14:03,567
What should we do?

359
00:14:03,667 --> 00:14:06,000
What if he runs into the
street and gets hit by a car?

360
00:14:06,024 --> 00:14:07,256
Please calm down.

361
00:14:07,733 --> 00:14:08,733
Okay?

362
00:14:10,367 --> 00:14:12,167
Let's search the neighborhood first.

363
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:14,167
Ma'am, please stay here.

364
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,333
Someone might contact us.

365
00:14:16,633 --> 00:14:17,633
But...

366
00:14:17,767 --> 00:14:18,767
It'll be fine.

367
00:14:19,467 --> 00:14:21,133
Leave it to us.

368
00:14:24,893 --> 00:14:25,893
Na-chan.

369
00:14:26,367 --> 00:14:27,367
Let's go.

370
00:14:30,633 --> 00:14:31,633
Let's move.

371
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:37,200
Rock!

372
00:14:37,433 --> 00:14:38,233
Rock!

373
00:14:38,333 --> 00:14:40,167
Hey, Rock!

374
00:14:40,267 --> 00:14:42,400
Na-chan, let's check over there.

375
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:45,700
Rock!

376
00:14:45,993 --> 00:14:46,993
Na-chan.

377
00:14:47,433 --> 00:14:48,633
Show her the picture.

378
00:14:50,267 --> 00:14:51,500
Have you seen this dog?

379
00:14:51,733 --> 00:14:53,267
Isn't that Rock?

380
00:14:53,367 --> 00:14:54,367
Do you know him?

381
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:56,467
I haven't seen him today.

382
00:14:56,733 --> 00:14:58,100
- I see.
- Yeah.

383
00:14:58,300 --> 00:14:59,300
Na-chan.

384
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:00,167
Rock!

385
00:15:00,267 --> 00:15:00,967
Thank you.

386
00:15:01,067 --> 00:15:02,067
No problem.

387
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:03,733
Rock!

388
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:06,400
Rock!

389
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:12,333
Rock!

390
00:15:14,433 --> 00:15:15,433
Rock!

391
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:28,500
Natsuki.

392
00:15:30,433 --> 00:15:31,433
Any luck?

393
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:32,900
Not a single clue.

394
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,000
What about you?

395
00:15:37,067 --> 00:15:38,067
Let's go look over there.

396
00:15:38,667 --> 00:15:40,500
If you hear anything, call me immediately.

397
00:15:40,707 --> 00:15:41,707
Thanks.

398
00:15:41,839 --> 00:15:42,333
We're counting on you.

399
00:15:42,357 --> 00:15:43,357
Got it.

400
00:15:52,786 --> 00:15:53,786
Na-chan.

401
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:55,360
Any news from the police?

402
00:15:59,653 --> 00:16:01,686
Let's go look over there.

403
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Na-chan?

404
00:16:12,107 --> 00:16:15,339
(Lost Property Report)
Why is he being treated as "lost property"?

405
00:16:16,467 --> 00:16:17,467
Huh?

406
00:16:19,700 --> 00:16:20,700
Didn't we just...

407
00:16:20,939 --> 00:16:23,139
fill out a "Lost Property Report"
at the police station?

408
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:26,500
Na-chan.

409
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:31,600
He's not just a thing.

410
00:16:34,059 --> 00:16:36,526
Rock... he's my family.

411
00:16:51,367 --> 00:16:52,367
Anyway.

412
00:16:54,213 --> 00:16:55,493
Let's go look for him right now.

413
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:00,500
Let's go.

414
00:17:08,733 --> 00:17:09,733
It'll be okay.

415
00:17:15,367 --> 00:17:17,167
Excuse me, have you two seen him?

416
00:17:17,267 --> 00:17:18,333
- No.
- No.

417
00:17:18,433 --> 00:17:19,600
We haven't.

418
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:20,967
I see.

419
00:17:21,233 --> 00:17:22,400
Thank you both.

420
00:17:29,467 --> 00:17:31,367
Where on earth did Rock go?

421
00:17:39,367 --> 00:17:41,400
Maybe we should hire a pet detective.

422
00:17:41,786 --> 00:17:45,720
You know, experts who specialize
in finding lost cats and dogs.

423
00:17:46,313 --> 00:17:48,180
I've seen them on TV.

424
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:51,033
(Pet Detective)
Found one.

425
00:18:05,533 --> 00:18:06,533
Huh?

426
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:07,700
What?

427
00:18:11,533 --> 00:18:12,567
Rock...

428
00:18:21,567 --> 00:18:22,567
Rock!

429
00:18:25,780 --> 00:18:26,780
Rock!

430
00:18:29,073 --> 00:18:30,140
Rock!

431
00:18:30,733 --> 00:18:32,333
Thank goodness, Rock!

432
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:33,800
Rio!

433
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:35,500
Oh.

434
00:18:35,533 --> 00:18:37,033
Huh, Sis?

435
00:18:39,099 --> 00:18:40,099
Why?

436
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:42,440
What do you mean, "why"?
I took him out for a walk.

437
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:43,500
What?

438
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,233
- Huh?
- What are you doing?

439
00:18:45,467 --> 00:18:46,667
Why are you crying?

440
00:18:48,633 --> 00:18:49,633
Because...

441
00:18:50,093 --> 00:18:51,759
Rock went missing.

442
00:18:51,819 --> 00:18:53,219
I couldn't find him anywhere.

443
00:18:54,526 --> 00:18:55,526
Huh?

444
00:18:55,667 --> 00:18:57,333
I have no idea what you're talking about.

445
00:18:57,357 --> 00:18:59,590
Rock wasn't at home, so
we were looking for him.

446
00:19:00,047 --> 00:19:00,747
Why?

447
00:19:00,887 --> 00:19:02,787
We thought you went to work, Rio.

448
00:19:02,906 --> 00:19:03,906
Yeah.

449
00:19:04,667 --> 00:19:06,033
I got my schedule mixed up.

450
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:09,120
Turns out I didn't have a shift
today, so I just came straight home.

451
00:19:09,367 --> 00:19:11,267
Then I saw Rock just chilling.

452
00:19:13,567 --> 00:19:16,533
Na-chan and Mom were so worried.

453
00:19:17,833 --> 00:19:18,833
Sorry, sorry.

454
00:19:18,926 --> 00:19:20,060
I'm so glad you're safe...

455
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:21,160
Rock.

456
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:25,067
Rock.

457
00:19:25,733 --> 00:19:27,067
You're okay.

458
00:19:27,533 --> 00:19:31,167
Rock, where on earth did you go?

459
00:19:31,367 --> 00:19:32,633
Thank goodness.

460
00:19:32,733 --> 00:19:34,300
I was so worried.

461
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:43,700
Are you okay?

462
00:19:44,700 --> 00:19:45,700
Yeah.

463
00:19:45,799 --> 00:19:46,799
I'm fine.

464
00:19:50,140 --> 00:19:53,506
I'll make sure to lock the door
properly when I go out from now on.

465
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:57,200
Even though it had
nothing to do with the lock.

466
00:19:57,667 --> 00:19:58,700
But let's do that anyway.

467
00:19:59,967 --> 00:20:01,067
Please do.

468
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:04,333
I guess growing up carefree in
the country made me a bit careless...

469
00:20:04,667 --> 00:20:06,633
But I definitely won't let it happen again.

470
00:20:09,533 --> 00:20:10,533
Rock.

471
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:11,133
Ah.

472
00:20:11,233 --> 00:20:13,233
By the way, where did Dad go?

473
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:15,133
He went drinking with Fuku-chan.

474
00:20:15,233 --> 00:20:16,233
Again?

475
00:20:16,633 --> 00:20:20,000
If Dad had been home, things
wouldn't have turned out like this.

476
00:20:20,100 --> 00:20:21,300
Exactly.

477
00:20:21,433 --> 00:20:22,433
Yeah.

478
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:25,100
Well...

479
00:20:25,333 --> 00:20:26,333
I see...

480
00:20:26,893 --> 00:20:28,759
Um... I'm really sorry.

481
00:20:31,567 --> 00:20:32,967
Right, let's help out.

482
00:20:33,067 --> 00:20:33,867
Okay.

483
00:20:33,967 --> 00:20:35,900
- Let's have some tea.
- Let's have another cup.

484
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,040
Huh, you're drinking more?

485
00:20:37,133 --> 00:20:38,467
Just a little bit.

486
00:20:38,567 --> 00:20:40,467
Don't drink too much.

487
00:20:56,467 --> 00:20:57,567
So fluffy.

488
00:21:06,013 --> 00:21:07,013
Ah.

489
00:21:07,233 --> 00:21:08,233
Oh, right.

490
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:09,240
Hmm?

491
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:10,253
Here you go.

492
00:21:10,277 --> 00:21:11,277
(Great Job)

493
00:21:14,567 --> 00:21:15,567
Huh?

494
00:21:15,633 --> 00:21:17,733
We didn't have class today.

495
00:21:18,367 --> 00:21:20,447
You worked really hard
looking for Rock, didn't you?

496
00:21:26,780 --> 00:21:27,780
You don't want it?

497
00:21:28,152 --> 00:21:29,152
No.

498
00:21:29,780 --> 00:21:31,113
This is for you.

499
00:21:32,180 --> 00:21:33,180
Huh?

500
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:36,633
Mom and I were totally panicking.

501
00:21:38,333 --> 00:21:39,333
If...

502
00:21:43,126 --> 00:21:44,893
If it weren't for So-chan...

503
00:21:45,433 --> 00:21:46,753
It would've been a real disaster.

504
00:21:48,600 --> 00:21:49,600
So.

505
00:21:50,567 --> 00:21:51,847
This is my way of saying thanks.

506
00:21:55,433 --> 00:21:58,100
I was only able to stay calm
because he's not my family.

507
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:00,600
Besides.

508
00:22:00,667 --> 00:22:02,533
You can finally pet Rock now.

509
00:22:03,273 --> 00:22:03,906
Yeah.

510
00:22:04,333 --> 00:22:06,133
He's so fluffy, it surprised me.

511
00:22:07,300 --> 00:22:08,333
You worked hard too.

512
00:22:10,533 --> 00:22:11,533
I see.

513
00:22:13,433 --> 00:22:14,967
I'll take it then.

514
00:22:15,780 --> 00:22:16,780
And...

515
00:22:18,380 --> 00:22:19,447
Here's this for you.

516
00:22:21,186 --> 00:22:22,186
No need.

517
00:22:22,253 --> 00:22:23,820
I don't have anywhere left to stick it.

518
00:22:24,567 --> 00:22:25,567
Then...

519
00:22:32,700 --> 00:22:33,700
Stick it here.

520
00:22:47,793 --> 00:22:49,327
I'm not a kid.

521
00:22:51,233 --> 00:22:52,367
Natsuki, are you asleep?

522
00:22:52,467 --> 00:22:53,233
I'm asleep.

523
00:22:53,333 --> 00:22:54,609
Huh, you're clearly still awake.

524
00:22:54,633 --> 00:22:55,633
What is it?

525
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:57,500
This is for you.

526
00:22:57,600 --> 00:22:58,733
I found this in Ueno.

527
00:22:59,100 --> 00:23:00,700
Since I'm always borrowing your clothes.

528
00:23:01,206 --> 00:23:02,406
Ta-da!

529
00:23:02,733 --> 00:23:04,133
Nice, I like it.

530
00:23:04,233 --> 00:23:05,233
Right?

531
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:08,567
Natsuki and I really
do like the same things.

532
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:09,867
No, we don't.

533
00:23:09,967 --> 00:23:11,207
Ah, let me borrow it next time.

534
00:23:14,667 --> 00:23:15,667
I...

535
00:23:16,153 --> 00:23:19,086
like the things my sister likes...

536
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:21,633
(This story is purely fictional)

537
00:23:21,733 --> 00:23:22,333
(Next Episode)

538
00:23:22,433 --> 00:23:24,393
(Getting Closer!?)
(A Sleepover on a Stormy Night)

539
00:23:24,433 --> 00:23:26,067
Just sleep here tonight.

540
00:23:26,090 --> 00:23:26,323
Huh?

541
00:23:26,500 --> 00:23:27,633
Fuku-chan.

542
00:23:27,733 --> 00:23:28,673
Do you live alone?

543
00:23:28,706 --> 00:23:28,939
Yes.

544
00:23:29,066 --> 00:23:31,816
(True Feelings Revealed Unintentionally)
So this is what having a family feels like.

545
00:23:31,927 --> 00:23:33,027
I need to calm down.

546
00:23:33,367 --> 00:23:34,676
(A Late-Night Secret Between the Two!?)
In front of Na-chan,

547
00:23:34,700 --> 00:23:37,567
I feel like I can be a bit more honest.
